## When can I get access to my money?
You can normally choose to take benefits from your Pension Portfolio at any time from the normal minimum pension age. This is currently age 55. From 6 April 2028 this will be age 57 unless you have a protected pension age. To find out more more visit aviva.co.uk/nmpa . You can't usually make any withdrawals before you reach the normal minimum pension age.
Once you reach the normal minimum pension age, you can choose to use all or part of your pension pot to provide an income, either through income drawdown or by buying a lifetime annuity. You may also be able to withdraw all, or part, of your pension pot as a cash lump sum.
People who can't continue working because of ill health may be able to start taking retirement benefits from their pension earlier than the normal minimum pension age.
When you set up your plan, you'll tell us your chosen retirement age (the age at which you want to start drawing benefits). You may change this at any time.

